  "worked_solution": "We note that $f=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nThe equation has the denominators $f,\\,2f,$ and $5f.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(f,2f,5f)=10f.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10f,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f+6}{f}-\\frac{3f+9}{5f} & =\\frac{f+2}{2f} \\\\ 10f(\\frac{f+6}{f}-\\frac{3f+9}{5f}) & =10f(\\frac{f+2}{2f}) \\\\ 10f\\cdot \\frac{f+6}{f}-10f\\cdot \\frac{3f+9}{5f} & =10f\\cdot \\frac{f+2}{2f} \\\\ 10\\cdot f\\cdot \\frac{f+6}{f}-2\\cdot 5f\\cdot \\frac{3f+9}{5f} & =5\\cdot 2f\\cdot \\frac{f+2}{2f} \\\\ 10\\cdot \\cancel{f}\\cdot \\frac{f+6}{\\cancel{f}}-2\\cdot \\cancel{5f}\\cdot \\frac{3f+9}{\\cancel{5f}} & =5\\cdot \\cancel{2f}\\cdot \\frac{f+2}{\\cancel{2f}} \\\\ 10(f+6)-2(3f+9) & =5(f+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $f,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10(f+6)-2(3f+9) & =5(f+2) \\\\ 10f+60-6f-18 & =5f+10 \\\\ 4f+42 & =5f+10 \\\\ -f & =-32 \\\\ f & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $f=0$ as a solution. But since $f=32\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $f=32.$",
